  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of Member States to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Establishment of three technical working groups (Employers&#x2019; Law; Legislative Reform; Dispute Resolution) to address outstanding comments of the ILO supervisory bodies on the application of C87 and C98 in Kazakhstan. Each of the technical working groups have met to discuss and implement the Action Plan on FOA and with ILO technical specialists. ILO Moscow Office recommended the establishment of technical tripartite working groups on each of the three key topics- regulation of employers&#x2019; groups; dispute resolution; and legislative reform, in order to provide technical guidance and engage in focussed technical discussions to resolve outstanding issues concerning FOA. Technical assistance to the groups have been provided as follows:
-	Series of three online meetings and discussions to identify and discuss gaps and reach agreement on ways forward
-	Tripartite working group on legislative reform: Comments and discussion on draft reforms of legislation; provision of comparative legislation; development and dissemination of technical guidance notes on trade union registrations and strikes
-	tripartite working group on dispute resolution : Facilitation of a self-assessment of collective disputes resolution; agreement on key steps and actions to address gaps; research and dissemination of research on improvements to collective dispute resolution system
-	tripartite working group on employers&#x2019; law: development of a concept for a law on employers&#x2019; organisations; dissemination of concept; training and technical guidance for the development of an employers&#x2019; law in line with C87.</narrative>
   </description>
